// The gate half of the `match` substitution leak, from the rejecting side. `v.item` is an `int32`; the
// destination is a `Reader<int32>`. That is a plain type error the author wrote, and KAMA must be the one
// to say so.
//
// It used to say nothing: the arm resolved `item` under the ENUM's binding for `T` — which is
// `Reader<int32>` — so the arm and the destination "agreed", `kama check` answered OK, and only clang
// refused the emitted C with `assigning to '_F…__Reader_int32' from incompatible type 'int32_t'`. A
// check/build disagreement plus invalid emitted C, the two things the 1.0 gate's own sentence names.
//
// The accepting side is `tests/match_generic_payload_member.kama`.
type value Reader<T> {
    public T item;
    public ctor make(T item) { this.item = item; return this; }
}
fn int32 main() {
    Optional<Reader<int32>> o = Optional::Some(value: Reader.make(item: 7));
    Reader<int32> wrong = match (o) { case Some(value: v): v.item; case None: Reader.make(item: 0); };
    return 0;
}
